ass", "lead_before": -5.91, "lead_after": -6.0, "points_lost": -0.09, "best": "pass"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Left-Edge Squeeze, Right-Side Recovery", "summary": "Opus 5.5 won as White by 6 points after two passes. Both sides gave away points in small amounts all game, and Opus 5.5 averaged 1.4 lost per move against the 10k's 1.7. The game turned on move 13, when the 10k's B6 lost 6.2 points, the only blunder on either side. After that White stayed ahead, and the endgame moves lost almost nothing.", "moments": [{"turn": 7, "text": "The 10k's G4 lost 4.5 points, taking Black's lead from -0.1 to -4.6. The engine preferred F4, and G4 left White room to build in the centre."}, {"turn": 13, "text": "The 10k's B6 is the game's one blunder. It lost 6.2 points and pushed Black's lead from -4.4 to -10.6, the biggest White advantage of the game. The engine wanted F3 instead of pressing on the left."}, {"turn": 14, "text": "Opus 5.5's H4 was its worst move at 4.5 points, and it let some of the lead back (-10.6 to -6.1). The engine preferred E7, but even after this White was well ahead."}, {"turn": 36, "text": "In the long exchange down the left and bottom, each side lost 2.5 to 3.9 points per move for a while, and the lead swung between about -8 and -4. Here Opus 5.5's A2 lost 3.9 points (-7.9 to -4.0), and the engine wanted A5 to be played."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "After the 10k took A5, Opus 5.5 answered at A4, the engine's own choice, losing 0.0 points. From here to the second pass no move on either side cost more than 0.1 points, and the lead held near -6.0, which is the W+6 result."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py prints groups and liberties of a pasted board, count.py does an area count of the current position, and the other commands only read and append to notes (games.md, CLAUDE.md); none of them chooses or ranks moves or looks ahead.", "stop": false}}